{"type":"text","timestamp":1794355344435,"sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","part":{"id":"prt_1c7e9b3de001WRvg5gdVN6ZxBZ","messageID":"msg_1c7e9a7da0011PR1W4WgLuaxxH","sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","type":"text","text":"<think>The npm view was blocked? Actually the first result shows a permission error about external_directory — that was for the pip download? No wait, the first result was for the npm command... The outputs seem swapped. The first result (npm view) shows the permission rule error — meaning running npm in /tmp/opencode was denied? Hmm, the error mentions \"external_directory\" deny pattern for \"*\" and allow for /tmp/opencode/*. The workdir was /tmp/opencode, so it should be allowed... but maybe the rule applies to the command's path patterns.\n\nSecond result: pip download failed creating /tmp/opencode/piptest — PermissionError. Maybe /tmp/opencode isn't writable? It says \"This directory has already been created, already exists, and is pre-approved\". Let me check permissions.\n\nLet me just run npm in /workspace/frontend instead.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794355344350,"end":1794355344381}}}
