{"type":"text","timestamp":1794355400290,"sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","part":{"id":"prt_1c7ea8e520012Z3DCjFpkracAC","messageID":"msg_1c7ea8518001wFo8x3fXvE1WIh","sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","type":"text","text":"<think>Now let me set up a local test environment: create a venv, install flask + gunicorn (from the lock/requirements), and run the app to test the API.\n\nNote: the sandbox can install packages from public registries. Let me create a venv in /workspace/.venv (gitignored? .dockerignore ignores .venv). Actually, I should avoid polluting the workspace. But there's no writable /tmp/opencode. Let me check if /tmp itself is writable (not /tmp/opencode).\n\nActually, pip install --user might work. Let me check whether flask is already installed system-wide.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794355400274,"end":1794355400287}}}
