{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794355433986,"sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","part":{"id":"prt_1c7eb11e7001A69gH2JTSnGxhZ","messageID":"msg_1c7eaff39001zugCyg0l933KMG","sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794355433986,"sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","part":{"id":"prt_1c7eb11ea001hH7GNsI9RVcDF3","messageID":"msg_1c7eaff39001zugCyg0l933KMG","sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","type":"text","text":"<think>Interesting: with require-hashes mode, transitive deps must also be pinned. The constraints file does pin them (blinker==1.9.0), but pip requires the pinned version in the *requirements* tree... Hmm, the error says blinker>=1.9.0 from flask's dependency isn't pinned. The constraints should apply. But in require-hashes mode pip checks that each requirement is pinned with ==; constraints should provide the pin... Apparently pip's check uses the \"identifier\" from the constraint to satisfy pinning? It says it isn't satisfied.\n\nHmm. The standard solution: make requirements.txt the fully-pinned hashed file (like pip-compile output), and the lock file the same content, or just use the lock file as the requirements file.\n\nThe Dockerfile: `if [ -f backend/requirements.lock ]; then pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock; else pip install -r backend/requirements.txt; fi`.\n\nSo requirements.txt must be installable with the lock as constraints. Options:\n1. Make requirements.txt the complete hashed pinned list (same as the lock). Then `-c lock` adds redundant constraints (same pins, same hashes) → works.\n2. Remove requirements.lock and keep requirements.txt as the full hashed list.\n\nOption 1 keeps the repo structure and the Dockerfile unchanged. Let me make requirements.txt identical to requirements.lock content (the full hashed transitive list). The lock has entries: blinker, click, flask, gunicorn, itsdangerous, jinja2, markupsafe, werkzeug — each with hashes.\n\nThen `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` → all pinned with hashes → require-hashes satisfied.\n\nBut wait: with require-hashes mode, pip requires hashes for each package and also that all deps are pinned — since the full list is present, that's satisfied. However, pip in require-hashes mode with a constraint file that also pins → fine.\n\nActually, would having requirements.txt == requirements.lock cause pip to complain about conflicting duplicates? No, constraints that match the requirement are fine.\n\nLet me test: copy lock to requirements.txt.\n\nHmm, but the lock file's structure has a header comment? Let me look at the beginningof the lock file.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794355433962,"end":1794355433982}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794355434023,"sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c7eb0f0774d1807a85db","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && head -30 backend/requirements.lock && grep -c \"^[a-z]\" backend/requirements.lock && grep \"^[a-z]\" backend/requirements.lock"},"output":"blinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n    --hash=sha256:ba0efaa9080b619ff2f3459d1d500c57bddea4a6b424b60a91141db6fd2f08bc\n    # via flask\nclick==8.5.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:255bc9599cf7748b4b1a446ccc735421bd08a2ae529a8b88597d3de5664ee360 \\\n    --hash=sha256:ba0d2089de75ea0310e2dde03160e6ca10009947fb95a182f9b54021bb272e34\n    # via flask\nflask==3.1.3 \\\n    --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94047b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb \\\n    --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n    # via -r requirements.txt\ngunicorn==26.2.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:62b864895d9ebff0b2f9867ba04fe811c93121596540830c9c916d0769668447 \\\n    --hash=sha256:bd249d0b3f7972f7432f0a6b6ff3b3ee2d129f70cd1ff6c09a9dd9e29a2b88e3\n    # via -r requirements.txt\nitsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:c6242fc49e35958c8b15141343aa660db5fc54d4f13a1db01a3f5891b98700ef \\\n    --hash=sha256:e0050c0b7da1eea53ffaf149c0cfbb5c6e2e2b69c4bef22c81fa6eb73e5f6173\n    # via flask\njinja2==3.1.6 \\\n    --hash=sha256:0137fb05990d35f1275a587e9aee6d56da821fc83491a0fb838183be43f66d6d \\\n    --hash=sha256:85ece4451f492d0c13c5dd7c13a64681a86afae63a5f347908daf103ce6d2f67\n    # via flask\nmarkupsafe==3.0.4 \\\n    --hash=sha256:007e1ffd9bf65bb6ee96df7b258fc632a4868dd5566037986c64781f35a36e98 \\\n    --hash=sha256:02fa4acbc6a3fc5c693c34d4dd8c1130b7fe99cc915181b0ddd6f72aeb296002 \\\n    --hash=sha256:03470d1a8268e692ecf79ecd565593e59d44219377a7ead61f1f1b94c1f7ff6b \\\n    --hash=sha256:04e7902ba80ee4bac1d50a549606527a1dcf0476cd81403db41099d3b60ec653 \\\n    --hash=sha256:051417f74bcaaefa316276e0ff723f541616ca51043d070da00249d9bddd3e3c \\\n8\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\nclick==8.5.0 \\\nflask==3.1.3 \\\ngunicorn==26.2.0 \\\nitsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\njinja2==3.1.6 \\\nmarkupsafe==3.0.4 \\\nwerkzeug==3.1.9 \\\n","metadata":{"output":"blinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d145f5445bf \\\n    --hash=sha256:ba0efaa9080b619ff2f3459d1d500c57bddea4a6b424b60a91141db6fd2f08bc\n    # via flask\nclick==8.5.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:255bc9599cf7748b4b1a446ccc735421bd08a2ae529a8b88597d3de5664ee360 \\\n    --hash=sha256:ba0d2089de75ea0310e2dde03160e6ca10009947fb95a182f9b54021bb272e34\n    # via flask\nflask==3.1.3 \\\n    --hash=sha256:0ef0e52b8a9cd932855379197dd8f94047b359ca0a78695144304cb45f87c9eb \\\n    --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n    # via -r requirements.txt\ngunicorn==26.2.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:62b864895d9ebff0b2f9867ba04fe811c93121596540830c9c916d0769668447 \\\n    --hash=sha256:bd249d0b3f7972f7432f0a6b6ff3b3ee2d129f70cd1ff6c09a9dd9e29a2b88e3\n    # via -r requirements.txt\nitsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:c6242fc49e35958c8b15141343aa660db5fc54d4f13a1db01a3f5891b98700ef \\\n    --hash=sha256:e0050c0b7da1eea53ffaf149c0cfbb5c6e2e2b69c4bef22c81fa6eb73e5f6173\n    # via flask\njinja2==3.1.6 \\\n    --hash=sha256:0137fb05990d35f1275a587e9aee6d56da821fc83491a0fb838183be43f66d6d \\\n    --hash=sha256:85ece4451f492d0c13c5dd7c13a64681a86afae63a5f347908daf103ce6d2f67\n    # via flask\nmarkupsafe==3.0.4 \\\n    --hash=sha256:007e1ffd9bf65bb6ee96df7b258fc632a4868dd5566037986c64781f35a36e98 \\\n    --hash=sha256:02fa4acbc6a3fc5c693c34d4dd8c1130b7fe99cc915181b0ddd6f72aeb296002 \\\n    --hash=sha256:03470d1a8268e692ecf79ecd565593e59d44219377a7ead61f1f1b94c1f7ff6b \\\n    --hash=sha256:04e7902ba80ee4bac1d50a549606527a1dcf0476cd81403db41099d3b60ec653 \\\n    --hash=sha256:051417f74bcaaefa316276e0ff723f541616ca51043d070da00249d9bddd3e3c \\\n8\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\nclick==8.5.0 \\\nflask==3.1.3 \\\ngunicorn==26.2.0 \\\nitsdangerous==2.2.0 \\\njinja2==3.1.6 \\\nmarkupsafe==3.0.4 \\\nwerkzeug==3.1.9 \\\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && head -30 backend/requirements.lock && grep -c \"^[a-z]\" backend/requirements.lock && grep \"^[a-z]\" backend/requirements.lock","time":{"start":1794355433973,"end":1794355433999}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7eb11ed001ahp4sNYDaSZyTb","sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","messageID":"msg_1c7eaff39001zugCyg0l933KMG"}}
