{"type":"text","timestamp":1794355629679,"sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","part":{"id":"prt_1c7ee0e62001OHDqdn34PmEdV7","messageID":"msg_1c7ee0024001qCpEgtt2Qhyk1c","sessionID":"ses_e38170798fferFf1mK07jkjW4e","type":"text","text":"<think>Now I need a tsconfig.json for TypeScript to work. The repo doesn't have one (minimal project). Vite's react template includes tsconfig.json with references to tsconfig.app.json and tsconfig.node.json. Let me create a simple single tsconfig.json:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUnusedLocals\": true,\n    \"noUnusedParameters\": true,\n    \"noFallthroughCasesInSwitch\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\", \"vite.config.ts\"]\n}\n```\n\nIncluding vite.config.ts requires node types for `defineConfig` — vite's own types include node? `vite` types reference node types (vite/client). `vite.config.ts` uses `defineConfig` from \"vite\" — it may need @types/node for `process` etc. Let me include only \"src\" to be safe, and add a separate check later.\n\nAlso `allowImportingTsExtensions` requires noEmit — fine.\n\nLet me create tsconfig.json and run typecheck.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794355629666,"end":1794355629676}}}
